prompt:
You are a sceptical financial analyst reviewing a forecast prepared by a colleague.

Given the following forecast for RELIANCE (base year 2021):
{
  "strategy": "baseline",
  "base_year": 2021,
  "forecast": [
    {
      "year": 2022,
      "revenue_cr": 167257,
      "net_income_cr": 21808,
      "eps": 17.19
    },
    {
      "year": 2023,
      "revenue_cr": 114100,
      "net_income_cr": 14876,
      "eps": 11.73
    },
    {
      "year": 2024,
      "revenue_cr": 77843,
      "net_income_cr": 10149,
      "eps": 8.0
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "FY2021 revenue declined sharply from FY2020 (336,097 to 245,050 crores), representing a YoY growth rate of approximately -27.1%. Similarly, net income grew marginally from 30,903 to 31,944 crores in FY2021 (+3.4%), but revenue contraction dominates the projection assumption. Applying the FY2021 revenue growth rate of -27.1% and net income growth rate of +3.4% forward yields rapidly declining revenue projections, which reflect the pandemic-driven downturn embedded in FY2021 figures; EPS is estimated using approximately 1,268 million shares outstanding derived from FY2021 reported EPS of 25.19 on net income of 31,944 crores."
}

Step 1: Identify the 3 most critical assumptions embedded in this forecast.
Step 2: For each assumption, describe one plausible scenario where it fails.
Step 3: Rate each assumption failure as Low / Medium / High risk to the forecast accuracy.
Step 4: Assign an overall confidence score from 0-100 (100 = completely certain).

Return ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "company": "<COMPANY>",
  "base_year": <YYYY>,
  "strategy": "<baseline|alt_strategy>",
  "assumptions": [
    {"assumption": "<text>", "failure_scenario": "<text>", "risk": "<Low|Medium|High>"}
  ],
  "confidence_score": <0-100>,
  "overall_critique": "<2 sentences>"
}

